MCQ and short-answer assessment rules:
- Do not use legacy assessment naming.
- assessmentType must be "MCQ".
- starterCode must be an empty string.
- expectedOutput must be an empty string.
- testCases must be an empty array.
- Include 3 to 6 MULTIPLE_CHOICE questions when MCQs are requested, unless the requested question count is lower. If MCQs are not requested, include none.
- Include 1 to 2 SHORT_ANSWER questions when short-answer questions are requested. If short-answer questions are not requested, include none.
- MULTIPLE_CHOICE questions should test practical job knowledge, debugging judgment, architecture tradeoffs, or scenario-based reasoning.
- Each MULTIPLE_CHOICE question must include 3 to 5 options.
- Exactly one option must have "correct": true for each MULTIPLE_CHOICE question.
- SHORT_ANSWER questions must focus on personality, communication, collaboration, prioritization, ambiguity, or work-style signals.
- SHORT_ANSWER questions are not automatically graded. Put interviewer guidance in correctAnswer and keep points low.
- All non-coding questions must use "language": "TEXT", empty starterCode, empty expectedOutput, and empty testCases.
- The top-level prompt should summarize the assessment goal for backward compatibility.
